<h2>A decade-old trial nearing its end</h2>
<p>The prosecution case is that in February 2016 the petitioner, a friend of the deceased, strangled her in his car after a quarrel connected to his imminent marriage, then hid the body in a ventilation shaft at his house. The body was recovered on 7 February 2016; the post-mortem recorded ligature strangulation. The car and bloodstained articles were recovered, and the FSL matched the victim&rsquo;s blood to the stains. Charges were framed under Sections 302 and 201 IPC in December 2016. The petitioner has been in custody since 2016, except for Covid-era interim bail between November 2020 and April 2023. By the time of this application — his third before the High Court, after four refusals by the trial court — 28 of 33 prosecution witnesses stood examined.</p>

<h2>The competing considerations</h2>
<table class="law">
